Adaptation: Go implementation of the vocab-parallel tensor-parallel decomposition
for fak's native engine (internal/model/tensor_parallel_vocab.go). Ported
mechanisms, in upstream terms:

  - VocabParallelEmbedding.forward: per-rank masked input lookup over the rank's
    contiguous vocabulary band (get_masked_input_and_mask), masked rows zeroed
    (masked_fill_), and the per-rank contributions AllReduce-summed
    (tensor_model_parallel_all_reduce). Each token id has exactly one owning
    rank, so the reduce is exact.
  - ParallelLMHead: the output-projection weight sharded along the vocabulary
    dimension; each rank computes its logits band and the bands are
    AllGather-concatenated in rank order (the sampler's
    tensor_model_parallel_all_gather in vllm/model_executor/layers/logits_processor.py).
  - get_sharded_to_full_mapping: the post-gather reindex of gathered logits.
    Upstream needs it to undo vocabulary padding and LoRA-added rows; fak's
    GGUF path has neither, so the mapping is the identity and the rank-order
    concat IS token-id order.

Divergences (fak adaptation, documented in the port file header):
  - Upstream pads the vocabulary to a multiple of DEFAULT_VOCAB_PADDING_SIZE
    (64) and requires exact divisibility (divide). fak reuses its validated
    TPPlan tiling (near-even contiguous bands, no empty shard), so no padding
    exists and the masked-input arithmetic degenerates to a single band test.
  - Upstream supports LoRA-added embeddings via the added_vocab_* shard
    indices; fak's serving path has no LoRA-added vocabulary rows, so those
    indices are absent from the port.
  - fak's head read is f32-resident only (the sharded matmul slices raw f32
    output rows); quant-resident heads fail closed, matching the existing
    tensor-parallel files' honesty contract.
